INT. CRUISE SHIP CALL CENTER - DAY

Cubicles bolted to the deck of a cruise ship. Portholes show open sea. A banner: "CUSTOMER DELIGHT AHOY."

BARB, forties, supervisor, paces. GREG, thirties, wears a headset. TRISH, twenties, files her nails. OMAR, fifties, stares at a screen. NIKOLAI, twenties, mops the floor. A figure in a tie sits at the end desk, introduced only as THE AUDITOR.

BARB
Greg, your call time is nine minutes.

GREG
It's the sea, Barb. Signal drifts.

TRISH
Barb, how do I unmute?

BARB
Trish, you're not muted.

CUSTOMER (V.O.)
(over headset)
Hello? Is this the help line? My cabin is on fire.

GREG
Please hold. Your call is important.

The Auditor stands. He strides to Barb.

THE AUDITOR
Barbara Finch?

BARB
It's Barb.

AUDITOR
It is now "Ms. Finch, Director of Delight."

BARB
(to the room)
I got promoted.

OMAR
(to himself)
Of course she did.

Nikolai drops the mop. The ship lurches. Greg pulls off his headset.

GREG
Barb? About that fire.
